From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 14:44:05 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] http: add Chrome fetch keep-alive header

Extend the existing pinned-curl HTTP/1.1 Connection default from
navigation weight 256 to default-fetch weight 220. Emit keep-alive once,
immediately after Host, matching local Chrome 154 recorder captures.

Keep the existing explicit-header/suppression, close/reuse, TE, WebSocket
and h2c guards intact. Internal/other requests, HTTP/1.0, HTTP/2, proxy
CONNECT, navigation headers, TLS and the macOS persona remain unchanged.

Validation: ReleaseFast build; all 1658 upstream tests; 22 temporary
native wire checks covering pooled classification reset, redirects,
overrides, both empty forms, close/reuse and upgrade/proxy handling.
Recorder page comparisons against Chrome and the previous binary cover
HTTP/2, HTTP/1.1 ALPN and no-ALPN fallback, cold and opted-in navigation
and no-store fetch. All 12 HTTP/1.1 fetches gain the correctly positioned
header; all 6 HTTP/2 fetches remain unchanged. Baseline TLS, other header
names/values/order and navigation are unchanged. The full repeated TLS
gate passes all eight scenarios with 20 processes per browser. Harness
TypeScript and Zig formatting checks pass. Reviewer found no issues.
No new unit tests.

References: fingerprint/README.md; patches/0059; pinned curl 8.22.0.
---
 tools/curl_http1_profile.zig | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/curl_http1_profile.zig b/tools/curl_http1_profile.zig
index d39159c..7ca88b2 100644
--- a/tools/curl_http1_profile.zig
+++ b/tools/curl_http1_profile.zig
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 // Brenno Flávio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
 
-//! Add Chrome's HTTP/1.1 navigation Connection default in pinned curl sources.
+//! Add Chrome's HTTP/1.1 navigation/fetch Connection default in pinned curl sources.
 const std = @import("std");
 
 pub fn main(init: std.process.Init) !void {
@@ -38,9 +38,10 @@ const after =
     \\      result = curlx_dyn_add(req, data->state.http_host);
     \\      if(!result)
     \\        result = curlx_dyn_addn(req, STRCONST("\r\n"));
-    \\      /* Weight 256 identifies Lightpanda's non-internal navigations.
+    \\      /* Weights 256/220 identify non-internal navigation/default fetch.
     \\       * Leave explicit headers and curl's late TE/upgrade handling alone. */
-    \\      if(!result && httpversion == 11 && data->set.weight == 256 &&
+    \\      if(!result && httpversion == 11 &&
+    \\         (data->set.weight == 256 || data->set.weight == 220) &&
     \\         !data->conn->bits.close && !data->set.reuse_forbid &&
     \\         !data->set.http_transfer_encoding &&
     \\         !(data->conn->scheme->protocol & (CURLPROTO_WS | CURLPROTO_WSS)) &&
